📘 1. Introduction
This document outlines the design and implementation plan for automating the monthly AMI rebuild process and BOXI application installation using Terraform and a GitLab CI/CD pipeline. This process ensures consistency, patching, and streamlined deployment of the BOXI environment.

🎯 2. Goals & Objectives
Automate monthly EC2 AMI refresh.

Install SAP BOXI application on top of the rebuilt AMI.

Ensure all required dependencies and configurations are baked into the instance.

Use GitLab CI/CD pipeline to drive the entire flow.

Ensure rollback and logging are available for traceability and audit.

🛠️ 3. Architecture Overview
Components Involved:

GitLab CI/CD: Orchestrates the rebuild process.

Terraform: Provisions AWS infrastructure.

Shell Scripts / Ansible: Handles BOXI installation and configuration.

Packer (Optional): Used for AMI creation (if building custom AMIs).

S3 / GitLab Artifacts: Stores logs, install packages, and configurations.

CloudWatch Logs: Captures system logs for monitoring.

🔁 4. Process Flow
Trigger (manual or scheduled in GitLab):

Triggered on 1st of every month or on demand.

Pipeline Steps:

Checkout Code

Validate Terraform

Build new AMI (optional via Packer or pre-created)

Destroy existing BOXI EC2 instance (optional depending on lifecycle policy)

Apply Terraform to create EC2 instance from new AMI

Run provisioners or Ansible to install BOXI

Health check validation

Notify stakeholders / Post to Slack / Email

Rollback Plan:

Use previous AMI or instance snapshot

Manual override pipeline stage for recovery

🧩 5. GitLab Pipeline Design (.gitlab-ci.yml)
yaml
